# Oswin Pell - the Wayfarer party's scholar (Act 1 campsite). Ettersnap lore,
# the memory rites, and the remembrance moss sidequest.
# Compile with:  scripts\Compile-Dialogue.ps1

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_Oswin

# The rites fire when the captured ettersnap is physically AT the camp:
# quest sets TSC_EttersnapCaught on acquisition, kind_on_map requires the
# creature on Oswin's map, and finishing the scene sets TSC_RitesDone
# (which also completes the TSC_Act1_Ettersnap quest via signal).
entry rites_ready if flag(TSC_EttersnapCaught) and not flag(TSC_RitesDone) and kind_on_map(TSC_Ettersnap)

== start ==
A reedy man sits cross-legged by a crate-desk, three books open at once, writing in a fourth. He doesn't look up.

"If you're a raider, the valuables are in the second crate and I'm busy. If you're the guild's courier: took you long enough, sit down, mind the inkwell."

* "Tell me about ettersnaps." -> lore
    if flag(TSC_MetParty)
* "Serra says you know how to catch this thing." -> moss
    if flag(TSC_MetParty) and not flag(TSC_GaveMoss)
* "What are these rites she mentioned?" -> rites
    if flag(TSC_MetParty)
* "What is your company hunting out here?" -> hunt_deflect
    if not flag(TSC_MetParty)
* "Teach me the Binder's school properly, Oswin." -> wizard_teaching
    if flag(TSC_OswinRespect) and not flag(TSC_OswinTaught)
* "Read me something, Oswin. Whatever's worth the ink tonight." -> reading
    if affinity(>=10) and not flag(TSC_OswinReading)
* "Just introducing myself." -> intro

== reading ==
Oswin looks up, suspicious, as if kindness were a forgery he's been trained to spot. Then he clears his throat and reads: a passage from the Chronicle, the one where the Nine Passes are named, each for the soldier who held it.

His voice is different when he reads. The squint goes out of it.

"Nobody has asked me to read aloud in eight years." He marks the page with a raven feather. "Ask again sometime, courier."

* "I will, scholar." -> end
    do flag(TSC_OswinReading); grant_xp(10)

# Pre-reveal: the hunt is Serra's story to tell, and Oswin knows it
== hunt_deflect ==
"Ah. No." He holds up one ink-stained finger without lifting his eyes from the page. "That story has an owner, and the owner is the woman by the firepit with the greatbow and the eight-week glare. Chain of command applies here, courier. It's the only discipline this company has left."

He dips the quill and keeps writing.

"Talk to Serra. Then come back, and I'll correct the parts she undersells. There will be several."

* "Fair enough. I'll ask the captain." -> end
* "Then tell me about yourself instead." -> intro

== wizard_teaching ==
Oswin sets down his quill with care.

"I have refused to teach eleven people, courier. Ten were fools and one was a warlord, which is a fool with a budget." He pulls a slim, hand-copied volume from the bottom of the crate-desk. "You quoted doctrine correctly in the field. That makes you the twelfth applicant and the first student."

Three evenings by the fire follow: sigil grammar, ward geometry, and the Binder's first exercise, which is holding a shape in the mind while distractions try their best to erase it.

* [Learn the Wizard's art] "I'll mind the inkwell, scholar." -> end
    if not flag(TSC_OswinTaught)
    do flag(TSC_OswinTaught); learn_class(TSC_Class_Wizard); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)
* "Another time. The hunt first." -> end

== intro ==
He finally looks up: ink-stained fingers, sharp eyes, the particular squint of a man who has read by firelight for eight weeks.

"Oswin Pell. Party scholar, rite-keeper, and the only member of this company who thinks 'evidence' is a full sentence. Now you know me. The books are better company, but you'll do."

* "Tell me about ettersnaps." -> lore
    if flag(TSC_MetParty)
* "How do we catch it?" -> moss
    if flag(TSC_MetParty) and not flag(TSC_GaveMoss)
* "What is it you're all hunting?" -> hunt_deflect
    if not flag(TSC_MetParty)
* "Good talk, Oswin." -> end

== lore ==
"Ettersnaps." He says the word the way other men say a lover's name. "The old kingdom called them grave-drinkers. They feed on the residue of memory, the stuff that soaks into ground and bone where the dead lie. Harmless to the living, priceless to scholarship, and nearly extinct because every warlord for eight centuries wanted one as an oracle."

He taps the open book: a woodcut of a spindly, quilled creature with too-knowing eyes.

"We're pretty sure ours has fed where the shard was lost. Everything the dead of that place saw (the shard, the hands that carried it) is in that creature like wine in a skin."

* "Pretty sure?" -> pretty_sure
* "And the rites pour the wine out." -> rites
* "How do we catch it?" -> moss
    if not flag(TSC_GaveMoss)
* [Arcana] "Memory as residue: that's Bindery doctrine. Aldruin's own school of magic." -> arcana_deep
    check Arcana 7 -> arcana_deep | arcana_shallow
* "The Chronicle of the Nine Passes mentions grave-drinkers. Twice, in the burial cantos." -> lore_deep
    if not flag(TSC_OswinRespect)
    check Lore 7 -> lore_deep | lore_shallow

== pretty_sure ==

"For now, it's our only lead."

* "And you know the rites to recover what it knows?" -> rites
* "How do we catch it?" -> moss
    if not flag(TSC_GaveMoss)
* [Arcana] "Memory as residue: that's Bindery doctrine. Aldruin's own school of magic." -> arcana_deep
    check Arcana 7 -> arcana_deep | arcana_shallow
* "The Chronicle of the Nine Passes mentions grave-drinkers. Twice, in the burial cantos." -> lore_deep
    if not flag(TSC_OswinRespect)
    check Lore 7 -> lore_deep | lore_shallow

== lore_deep ==
Oswin's quill stops mid-word.

"The burial cantos. Which nobody reads, because the Chronicle's a doorstop and the cantos are in the old meter." He leans forward, delighted despite himself. "Yes: twice. Once as omen, once as *inventory*. You've actually read it. Courier, I take back a full third of what I assumed about you."

* "Only a third, scholar?" -> end
    do flag(TSC_OswinRespect); grant_xp(25); affinity(TSC_Npc_Oswin, +5)

== lore_shallow ==
"The Chronicle of the Nine Passes." Oswin's eyes narrow. "Which canto, courier? Because the Chronicle has no burial cantos; you're thinking of the Lay of the Cold Hearth, and misquoting it at that. Points for ambition. None for scholarship."

* "Worth a try. Tell me more about the creature, then." -> lore

== arcana_deep ==
Oswin's quill stops. He looks at you the way he looks at a rare book.

"*Somebody* reads. Yes, the Binder's school held that memory outlives the mind that made it, the way heat outlives the fire. The crown itself was built on that doctrine: nine shards, each one holding... hm." He catches himself, glances toward Serra's fire, lowers his voice. "Each one holding more than metal. Ask me again when the ettersnap has spoken. I dislike being wrong in front of the well-read."

* "I'll hold you to it, scholar." -> end
    do flag(TSC_OswinRespect); grant_xp(25); affinity(TSC_Npc_Oswin, +5)

== arcana_shallow ==
"Bindery doctrine! Everyone's a scholar." He snorts and returns to his writing. "The Binder's school is a century of corrupted copies and wishful marginalia. Mind the rites, courier, and leave the doctrine to people with reference libraries."

* "As you say, Oswin." -> end

== rites ==
"The Rite of the Poured Cup. Some incantations, a circle of grave-iron, and a very patient singer, which will be me, as Serra's singing frightens horses. Done right, the creature dreams aloud and we transcribe. Done wrong, the memories curdle and we learn nothing."

He fixes you with the squint.

"Which is why the creature must come back *alive*. No clubs, no heroics."

* "Then tell me about the moss." -> moss
    if not flag(TSC_GaveMoss)
* "Alive. Understood." -> end

== moss ==
"Remembrance moss." He pulls a sketch: pale fronds, silver veins. "Grows only where the dead lie long undisturbed, and to an ettersnap it is a lit feast in a dark room. They cannot resist it. The mosskeepers of the old kingdom farmed it in cold barrows, and one of their barrows stands not a day from this fire."

He marks your map with an ink-stained thumb.

"Bring back an armful of it and the creature will follow you home like a lamb. Go without it and you can try patience against a thing that has outwaited kingdoms. The barrow *will* be tenanted. They always are."

* "I'll fetch your moss, scholar." -> end
    do flag(TSC_GaveMoss); give_quest(TSC_Side_Moss)
* "We'll see if it's needed." -> end
    do affinity(-5)

# Bridge into the rite: entered automatically (see entry above) once the
# living ettersnap is on Oswin's map. Backing out is safe; the entry
# re-fires next time you talk to him.
== rites_ready ==

Oswin is on his feet before you've said a word, ink abandoned mid-sentence, staring past you at the ettersnap with the expression most men reserve for royalty or ghosts.

"You actually... eight weeks, and there it is. Drinking half the pass's dead like wine in a skin." He is already pulling grave-iron stakes from the bottom of a crate, counting under his breath. "Keep it calm. Keep it CLOSE. I need an hour to raise the circle, and then, courier, we are going to listen to a creature remember."

* "Begin your rite, scholar. We'll keep it settled." -> rites_1
* "An hour, then. I'll not go far." -> end

== rites_1 ==

It takes a while, but eventually Oswin's preparations are complete. He finishes one last incantation, and then begins singing in a language you've never heard before.

His voice is surprisingly good.

* Sit and listen. -> rites_2

== rites_2 ==

You sit silently listening, watching the sedated ettersnap in the center of the circle. You see its chest just barely rise and fall with long, slow breaths.

Eventually, something begins to appear faintly above the ettersnap. It starts out as a dark splotch in your vision, but quickly grows to a full-on hallucination.

It shows what is very clearly the inside of a sanguophage's crypt. Next to a sleeping sanguophage is unmistakably a piece of the shattered crown. You've never seen a shard before, but you instinctively know it to be true.
The visage then shifts to an outdoor setting - a serene lake fed by a waterfall, surrounded by cedar trees.

Then, just as quickly as it came, the vision is gone.

* "Well, that was something." -> rites_3

== rites_3 ==

"Good news and bad news," Oswin says.

"Bad news first: I've no clue where that crypt is."

* "And the good news?" -> rites_4b
* "But the crown is there! We saw it!" -> rites_4a

== rites_4a ==

"Yep. So two pieces of good news, I guess."

* "What's the other?" -> rites_4b

== rites_4b ==

"I know where that oasis is. I've been there. And it's not far from a village."

* "That's where we're headed next, then." -> rites_5
* "Someone at that village might know something that could help us." -> rites_5

== rites_5 ==

"Agreed. I'll mark it on your map. If you don't mind, though, Serra and I will pack up camp and meet you there."

* "You're not coming with us?" -> rites_6
* "Stay safe, you two." -> end
    do flag(TSC_RitesDone); signal(TSC_Act1_Ettersnap, TSC_RitesPerformed); grant_xp(250); affinity(+5)

== rites_6 ==

"Nope. I don't want to slow you down - not when we're this close. When you get there, talk to the locals. Don't spook them, though. We probably need their help."

* "On my way." -> end
    do flag(TSC_RitesDone); signal(TSC_Act1_Ettersnap, TSC_RitesPerformed); grant_xp(250); affinity(+5)
